// Brought to u by MidManStudio
// =============================================================================
// NPM CI TESTER — NON-WORKFLOW FILES ONLY  ·  DixScript v1.0.0
// =============================================================================
// Corrected from the previous drop of the same name: that one had
// .github/workflows/npm-test.yml and .github/workflows/wasm-npm-publish.yml
// in it. Workflow files can NEVER go through this Action -- apply-replacements.yml
// grants the underlying job only `permissions: contents: write`, not
// `workflows: write`, and generate-structure.yml (mdix-scaffold, the
// reusable workflow that actually does the `git push`) caps at the same
// `contents: write` on its own end too -- so even granting workflows:
// write on the caller side here wouldn't be enough on its own; the callee
// would need it too, and that's a different repo. GitHub's server-side
// push protection rejects the WHOLE commit if any file in it touches
// .github/workflows/, which means the two harmless files below would have
// failed to land as well, dragged down by the same push. Confirmed by
// reading both workflows directly, not guessed.
//
// The 2 workflow files (new npm-test.yml + the wasm-npm-publish.yml fix)
// are delivered separately as plain files instead -- paste those directly
// through GitHub's own web file editor. A human editing through the
// website has full permissions regardless of this restriction; it only
// applies to automated pushes using the Actions-issued GITHUB_TOKEN.
//
// Only 2 files here, both non-yml, both nested (.github/...) -- no
// overrides:: needed.
// =============================================================================

@CONFIG(
  version    -> "1.0.0"
  author     -> "MidManStudio"
  debug_mode -> "off"
)

@DATA(
  description = "npm-test-template.html + landing-index.html (npm card) only -- the 2 workflow files from this same batch are delivered separately as plain files, not through this Action"
  target_root = "."
)
